<title>USA: Paravant Computer Q1 Dec 31 full results.</title>
<headline>Paravant Computer Q1 Dec 31 full results.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE, Fla. 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							    December 31,</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p> Revenues				    $1,931,092	$765,274</p>
<p> Cost of revenues			   1,054,127	 306,179</p>
<p> Gross profit				   876,965	 459,095</p>
<p> Selling and administrative expense     997,983	 926,469</p>
<p> Loss from operations		     (121,018)     (467,374)</p>
<p>Other income (expense):</p>
<p>   Miscellaneous income/expense		 102	 (1,259)</p>
<p> Interest expense			    (44,213)     (125,145)</p>
<p> Loss before income taxes		 (165,129)     (593,778)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit			    57,570	 223,439</p>
<p> Net loss				     (107,559)     (370,339)</p>
<p> Loss per share				   (.01)	   (.08)</p>
<p> Weighted average number of shares   12,825,364     4,500,000</p>
<p>Note: Per share calculations for all periods give effect to the initial public offering of 1,150,000 shares of Paravant common stock and 1,610,000 redeemable warrants on June 3, 1996, and the three-for-one common stock split effected at the close of business on July 25, 1996.</p>
<p>When dilutive, stock options and warrants are included as share equivalents.</p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Paravant Computer Systems Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
